IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, part sfad: Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (4), ss 277 to 282: the offer made using an offer information statement (s 277),
-- international debentures (s 278), debentures offered by the Government or an international financial institution (s 279),
-- offers made using an automated teller machine or other electronic means (s 280), the power to require information (s 280A),
-- revocation of an exemption (s 281) and the declaration that liability is preserved (s 282) (lines 44588-44989 of SFA2001.txt).
-- Imports prelude, daydate, sfa-core and sfa-periods (every period is counted by sfa-periods, never here).
--
-- How to read a function in this module: as in sfad-nocons-small-private.l4 (JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING where it does not say).
--   Section 277(1) says that Subdivisions (2) and (3) (other than section 257) "do not apply to an offer ... if the following conditions are satisfied".
--   Each condition is its own function; the function for subsection (1) takes the answers of the conditions as MAYBE BOOLEAN inputs, with the answer of subsection (1A).
--   What the Authority may prescribe (excluded securities, electronic means, requirements, the form and content of the statement) is an INPUT.
--   Terms of the keel (approved exchange, business trust, trustee-manager, subsidiary, capital markets services licence, exempt person) are asked as plain facts.
--   "-- FORK" lines are collected into the fork register of NOTES.md.

§ `s 277(1AA): units or shares treated as listed through SDRs`

-- src:44667 | (1AA) For the purposes of subsection (1)(a), units in a business
-- src:44668 | trust or shares of a corporation are treated as being listed for quotation
-- src:44673 | on an approved exchange if SDRs with units in the business trust or
-- src:44674 | shares of the corporation (as the case may be) as the underlying
-- src:44675 | securities are listed for quotation on the approved exchange.
@ref s 277(1AA) (src:44667-44675)
GIVEN
    `the units in the business trust or the shares of the corporation are listed for quotation on the approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the units in the business trust, or the shares of the corporation (as the case may be), listed for quotation on the approved exchange?
    `SDRs with the units in the business trust or the shares of the corporation as the underlying securities are listed for quotation on the approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are sponsored depositary receipts ("SDRs") with the units in the business trust, or the shares of the corporation (as the case may be), as the underlying securities listed for quotation on the approved exchange?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1AA) the units in the business trust or the shares of the corporation are treated as being listed for quotation on an approved exchange` MEANS
    IF `the units in the business trust or the shares of the corporation are listed for quotation on the approved exchange` OR `SDRs with the units in the business trust or the shares of the corporation as the underlying securities are listed for quotation on the approved exchange`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "are treated as being listed for quotation on an approved exchange if SDRs with units in the business trust or shares of the corporation"
    -- FORK s277-1AA | s 277(1)(a) | `s 277(1AA) the units in the business trust or the shares of the corporation are treated as being listed for quotation on an approved exchange` | took NOTHING where neither the units or shares nor the SDRs are listed (a deeming that extends "listed"; it does not say they are not listed otherwise) | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {IN-SHORT} ("includes" and an extension answer NOTHING); the listing question itself is the first input, so a caller who says neither is listed gets NOTHING here and JUST FALSE from the paragraph

§ `s 277(1)(a): the securities or contracts offered`


-- src:44598 | (a) the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts
-- src:44599 | are —
-- src:44601 | (i) units or derivatives of units in a business trust, issued
-- src:44602 | by a trustee‑manager in its capacity as
-- src:44603 | trustee‑manager of the business trust, where the
-- src:44604 | business trust is one the units of which are listed for
-- src:44605 | quotation on an approved exchange;
@ref s 277(1)(a)(i) (src:44598-44605)
GIVEN
    `the securities or contracts are units or derivatives of units in a business trust, issued by a trustee-manager in its capacity as trustee-manager of the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts units, or derivatives of units, in a business trust, issued by a trustee-manager in its capacity as trustee-manager of the business trust?
    `the units of the business trust are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 277(1AA) says` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the units of the business trust listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs with the units as the underlying securities as section 277(1AA) says? (Pass TRUE if what the function for section 277(1AA) answers is JUST TRUE.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1)(a)(i) the securities or contracts are units or derivatives of units in a listed business trust` MEANS
    IF `the securities or contracts are units or derivatives of units in a business trust, issued by a trustee-manager in its capacity as trustee-manager of the business trust` AND `the units of the business trust are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 277(1AA) says`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the following conditions are satisfied"

-- src:44609 | (ia) SDRs the underlying securities of which are units in
-- src:44610 | a business trust issued by a trustee‑manager in its
-- src:44611 | capacity as trustee‑manager of the business trust,
-- src:44616 | where the business trust is one the units of which are
-- src:44617 | listed for quotation on an approved exchange;
@ref s 277(1)(a)(ia) (src:44609-44617)
GIVEN
    `the securities are SDRs the underlying securities of which are units in a business trust issued by a trustee-manager in its capacity as trustee-manager of the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities SDRs the underlying securities of which are units in a business trust issued by a trustee-manager in its capacity as trustee-manager of the business trust?
    `the units of the business trust are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 277(1AA) says` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the units of the business trust listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs with the units as the underlying securities as section 277(1AA) says? (Pass TRUE if what the function for section 277(1AA) answers is JUST TRUE.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1)(a)(ia) the securities are SDRs of a listed business trust` MEANS
    IF `the securities are SDRs the underlying securities of which are units in a business trust issued by a trustee-manager in its capacity as trustee-manager of the business trust` AND `the units of the business trust are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 277(1AA) says`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the following conditions are satisfied"

-- src:44621 | (ii) securities or securities-based derivatives contracts
-- src:44622 | (other than those mentioned in sub‑paragraph (i) and
-- src:44623 | SDRs) issued by a corporation the shares of which
-- src:44624 | are listed for quotation on an approved exchange; or
@ref s 277(1)(a)(ii) (src:44621-44624)
GIVEN
    `the securities or contracts are those mentioned in sub-paragraph (i) or are SDRs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts those mentioned in section 277(1)(a)(i) (units or derivatives of units in a business trust issued by a trustee-manager) or SDRs?
    `the securities or contracts are issued by a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts issued by a corporation?
    `the shares of the corporation are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 277(1AA) says` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares of the corporation listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs with the shares as the underlying securities as section 277(1AA) says? (Pass TRUE if what the function for section 277(1AA) answers is JUST TRUE.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1)(a)(ii) the securities or contracts are issued by a corporation whose shares are listed` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the securities or contracts are those mentioned in sub-paragraph (i) or are SDRs`) AND `the securities or contracts are issued by a corporation` AND `the shares of the corporation are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 277(1AA) says`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the following conditions are satisfied"

-- src:44630 | (iii) SDRs the underlying securities of which are
-- src:44631 | securities issued by a corporation (other than those
-- src:44632 | mentioned in sub‑paragraph (i)), where the
-- src:44633 | corporation is one the shares of which are listed for
-- src:44634 | quotation on an approved exchange;
@ref s 277(1)(a)(iii) (src:44630-44634)
GIVEN
    `the securities are SDRs the underlying securities of which are securities issued by a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities SDRs the underlying securities of which are securities issued by a corporation?
    `the underlying securities are those mentioned in sub-paragraph (i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the underlying securities units or derivatives of units in a business trust issued by a trustee-manager (those mentioned in section 277(1)(a)(i))?
    `the shares of the corporation are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 277(1AA) says` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares of the corporation listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs with the shares as the underlying securities as section 277(1AA) says? (Pass TRUE if what the function for section 277(1AA) answers is JUST TRUE.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1)(a)(iii) the securities are SDRs of a listed corporation` MEANS
    IF `the securities are SDRs the underlying securities of which are securities issued by a corporation` AND (NOT `the underlying securities are those mentioned in sub-paragraph (i)`) AND `the shares of the corporation are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, counting SDRs as section 277(1AA) says`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the following conditions are satisfied"

-- src:44598 | (a) the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts
@ref s 277(1)(a) (src:44598-44598)
GIVEN
    `the answer of sub-paragraph (i)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 277(1)(a)(i) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the answer of sub-paragraph (ia)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 277(1)(a)(ia) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the answer of sub-paragraph (ii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 277(1)(a)(ii) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the answer of sub-paragraph (iii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 277(1)(a)(iii) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1)(a) the securities or contracts are of a kind the paragraph names` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the answer of sub-paragraph (i)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the answer of sub-paragraph (ia)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the answer of sub-paragraph (ii)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the answer of sub-paragraph (iii)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the answer of sub-paragraph (i)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the answer of sub-paragraph (ia)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the answer of sub-paragraph (ii)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the answer of sub-paragraph (iii)` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a sub-paragraph is not answered and no answered sub-paragraph holds
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the following conditions are satisfied"
    -- FORK s277-1a | s 277(1)(a) | `s 277(1)(a) the securities or contracts are of a kind the paragraph names` | took the four sub-paragraphs as alternatives (the rendering ends (i) and (ia) with a semicolon and a comma, (ii) with "; or" and (iii) with a semicolon, and no "and" joins them) | other reading all four must hold (which no offer can satisfy, since (i) and (ii) exclude each other) | licence the text's own words: "(ii) ... (other than those mentioned in sub-paragraph (i) and SDRs) ... ; or"

§ `s 277(1)(aa) and (ab): units and derivatives of units`

-- src:44638 | (aa) if the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts
-- src:44639 | are units of shares or units of debentures, the issuer of the
-- src:44640 | units is the issuer of those shares or debentures, as the case
-- src:44641 | may be;
@ref s 277(1)(aa) (src:44638-44641)
GIVEN
    `the securities or contracts are units of shares or units of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts units of shares or units of debentures?
    `the issuer of the units is the issuer of those shares or debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the issuer of the units the issuer of those shares or debentures, as the case may be?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1)(aa) the issuer of the units is the issuer of the shares or debentures` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the securities or contracts are units of shares or units of debentures`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the issuer of the units is the issuer of those shares or debentures`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the following conditions are satisfied"
    -- FORK s277-1aa | s 277(1)(aa) | `s 277(1)(aa) the issuer of the units is the issuer of the shares or debentures` | took JUST TRUE where the securities are not units of shares or of debentures (a condition that begins "if the securities ... are units" has nothing to fail when its own antecedent is unmet) | other reading NOTHING (the paragraph is silent about other securities) | licence no ruling covers a conditional condition: assumed, not ruled

-- src:44645 | (ab) if the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts
-- src:44646 | are derivatives of units in a business trust, the issuer of the
-- src:44647 | derivatives is the issuer of those units in the business trust;
@ref s 277(1)(ab) (src:44645-44647)
GIVEN
    `the securities or contracts are derivatives of units in a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts derivatives of units in a business trust?
    `the issuer of the derivatives is the issuer of those units in the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the issuer of the derivatives the issuer of those units in the business trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1)(ab) the issuer of the derivatives is the issuer of the units in the business trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the securities or contracts are derivatives of units in a business trust`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the issuer of the derivatives is the issuer of those units in the business trust`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the following conditions are satisfied"
    -- FORK s277-1ab | s 277(1)(ab) | `s 277(1)(ab) the issuer of the derivatives is the issuer of the units in the business trust` | took JUST TRUE where the securities are not derivatives of units in a business trust (a condition that begins "if" has nothing to fail when its own antecedent is unmet) | other reading NOTHING (the paragraph is silent about other securities) | licence no ruling covers a conditional condition: assumed, not ruled

§ `s 277(1)(b), (1)(c), (1A) and (1B): the statement, how the offer is made, the period and the machine conditions`

-- src:44651 | (b) an offer information statement relating to the offer which
-- src:44652 | complies with such requirements as to form and content as
-- src:44653 | may be prescribed by regulations made under section 341
-- src:44654 | is lodged with the Authority;
@ref s 277(1)(b) (src:44651-44654)
GIVEN
    `an offer information statement relating to the offer is lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an offer information statement relating to the offer lodged with the Authority?
    `the offer information statement complies with such requirements as to form and content as the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offer information statement comply with the requirements as to form and content that the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341 (as the Authority has modified them under section 277(2), where it has)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1)(b) an offer information statement complying with the prescribed requirements is lodged with the Authority` MEANS
    IF `an offer information statement relating to the offer is lodged with the Authority` AND `the offer information statement complies with such requirements as to form and content as the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the following conditions are satisfied"

-- src:44746 | (1B) The conditions mentioned in subsections (1)(c)(ii) and
-- src:44747 | (1AC)(b)(ii) are —
-- src:44749 | (a) the offer is made using any automated teller machine or
-- src:44750 | such other electronic means as the Authority may
-- src:44751 | prescribe;
-- src:44753 | (b) the automated teller machine or prescribed electronic
-- src:44754 | means indicates to a prospective subscriber or buyer —
-- src:44756 | (i) how the prospective subscriber or buyer can obtain,
-- src:44757 | or arrange to receive, a copy of the offer information
-- src:44758 | statement in respect of the offer; and
-- src:44760 | (ii) that the prospective subscriber or buyer should read
-- src:44761 | the offer information statement before submitting an
-- src:44762 | application,
-- src:44764 | (b) before enabling the prospective subscriber or buyer to
-- src:44765 | submit any application to subscribe for or purchase
-- src:44766 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts; and
-- src:44768 | (c) the person making the offer complies with such other
-- src:44769 | requirements as the Authority may prescribe.
@ref s 277(1B) (src:44746-44769)
GIVEN
    `the offer is made using an automated teller machine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made using an automated teller machine?
    `the offer is made using other electronic means that the Authority has prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made using electronic means, other than an automated teller machine, that the Authority has prescribed?
    `the machine or the prescribed electronic means indicates to a prospective subscriber or buyer how to obtain, or arrange to receive, a copy of the offer information statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the automated teller machine or the prescribed electronic means indicate to a prospective subscriber or buyer how they can obtain, or arrange to receive, a copy of the offer information statement in respect of the offer?
    `the machine or the prescribed electronic means indicates to a prospective subscriber or buyer that they should read the offer information statement before submitting an application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the automated teller machine or the prescribed electronic means indicate to a prospective subscriber or buyer that they should read the offer information statement before submitting an application?
    `the indications are given before enabling the prospective subscriber or buyer to submit any application to subscribe for or purchase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those indications given before the prospective subscriber or buyer is enabled to submit any application to subscribe for or purchase securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the person making the offer complies with such other requirements as the Authority may prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person making the offer comply with such other requirements as the Authority has prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1B) all the conditions are satisfied` MEANS
    IF (`the offer is made using an automated teller machine` OR `the offer is made using other electronic means that the Authority has prescribed`) AND `the machine or the prescribed electronic means indicates to a prospective subscriber or buyer how to obtain, or arrange to receive, a copy of the offer information statement` AND `the machine or the prescribed electronic means indicates to a prospective subscriber or buyer that they should read the offer information statement before submitting an application` AND `the indications are given before enabling the prospective subscriber or buyer to submit any application to subscribe for or purchase` AND `the person making the offer complies with such other requirements as the Authority may prescribe`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "all the conditions in subsection (1B) are satisfied"
    -- FORK s277-1B | s 277(1B)(b) | `s 277(1B) all the conditions are satisfied` | took the second "(b)" in the rendering ("(b) before enabling the prospective subscriber or buyer to submit any application ...") as the end of paragraph (b), which the text's own sentence runs on to: the two indications of (b)(i) and (b)(ii) are given "before enabling" the application | other reading a separate fourth condition, which changes nothing for the answer (it is asked as its own input either way) | licence the text's own words: "(ii) that the prospective subscriber or buyer should read the offer information statement before submitting an application, (b) before enabling the prospective subscriber or buyer to submit any application"

-- src:44656 | (c) either —
-- src:44658 | (i) the offer is made in, or accompanied by, the offer
-- src:44659 | information statement mentioned in paragraph (b); or
-- src:44661 | (ii) all the conditions in subsection (1B) are satisfied.
@ref s 277(1)(c) (src:44656-44661)
GIVEN
    `the offer is made in, or accompanied by, the offer information statement mentioned in paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made in, or accompanied by, the offer information statement mentioned in section 277(1)(b)?
    `the answer of subsection (1B)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 277(1B) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1)(c) the offer is made in or accompanied by the statement, or all the conditions in subsection (1B) are satisfied` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the offer is made in, or accompanied by, the offer information statement mentioned in paragraph (b)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the answer of subsection (1B)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the answer of subsection (1B)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the conditions of subsection (1B) are satisfied is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "either — (i) the offer is made in, or accompanied by, the offer information statement"

-- src:44679 | (1A) Subsection (1) only applies to an offer of securities or
-- src:44680 | securities‑based derivatives contracts referred to in that subsection
-- src:44681 | made within a period of 6 months from the date the offer information
-- src:44682 | statement relating to that offer is lodged with the Authority.
@ref s 277(1A) (src:44679-44682)
GIVEN
    `an offer information statement relating to the offer has been lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an offer information statement relating to the offer been lodged with the Authority?
    `the day the offer information statement was lodged` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the offer information statement relating to the offer lodged with the Authority?
    `the day the offer is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the offer made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1A) the offer is made within the period of 6 months from the date the offer information statement is lodged` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an offer information statement relating to the offer has been lodged with the Authority`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "from the date the offer information statement relating to that offer is lodged with the Authority"
        IF (`the day the offer is made` AT LEAST `the day the offer information statement was lodged`) AND (`the day the offer is made` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the day the offer information statement was lodged` 6 Months))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) only applies to an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts referred to in that subsection made within a period of 6 months"
    -- FORK s277-1A | s 277(1A) | `s 277(1A) the offer is made within the period of 6 months from the date the offer information statement is lodged` | took the 6 months as beginning with the day of lodgment (keel P10, "beginning with") and JUST FALSE outside the period, because "only applies" closes the gate in the text's own words; NOTHING where no statement has been lodged (there is no date to count from) | other reading the period starts the day after lodgment (keel P1, "from") | licence {P-a} (a period the text fixes in its own words) and {IN-SHORT} ("only")

-- src:44590 | 277.—(1) Subject to subsection (1A), Subdivisions (2) and (3) of
-- src:44591 | this Division (other than section 257) do not apply to an offer of
-- src:44592 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts (not being such
-- src:44593 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts as may be
-- src:44594 | prescribed by regulations made under section 341), whether by
-- src:44595 | means of a rights issue or otherwise, if the following conditions are
-- src:44596 | satisfied:
@ref s 277(1) (src:44590-44596)
GIVEN
    `the securities or contracts are of a kind that the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a kind that the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341 as outside this exemption?
    `the answer of paragraph (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 277(1)(a) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the answer of paragraph (aa)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 277(1)(aa) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the answer of paragraph (ab)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 277(1)(ab) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the answer of paragraph (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 277(1)(b) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the answer of paragraph (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 277(1)(c) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the answer of subsection (1A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 277(1A) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the securities or contracts are of a kind that the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "not being such securities or securities-based derivatives contracts as may be prescribed by regulations made under section 341"
        IF `the answer of subsection (1A)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) only applies"
        IF (`the answer of paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the answer of paragraph (aa)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the answer of paragraph (ab)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the answer of paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the answer of paragraph (c)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the following conditions are satisfied"
        IF (`the answer of paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of paragraph (aa)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of paragraph (ab)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of paragraph (c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of subsection (1A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a condition, or the period of subsection (1A), is not answered
    -- FORK s277-1 | s 277(1) | `s 277(1) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` | took NOTHING for securities or contracts the Authority has prescribed as outside the exemption (the content of the prescription is in regulations, outside the text; "not being such ... as may be prescribed" is a scope limit with no "only") and JUST FALSE where a condition fails or the six months of subsection (1A) have run | other reading JUST FALSE for the prescribed securities | licence {P-c} for the prescribed securities, {IN-SHORT} ("if", "only") for the conditions
    -- FORK s277-1-257 | s 277(1) | `s 277(1) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` | took "(other than section 257)" as not touched by this function: no rule about section 257, which is Subdivision (2)'s and another part's, is encoded here, so the answer says only that Subdivisions (2) and (3) do not apply, leaving section 257 for the caller to apply | other reading a flag for the caller that section 257 still applies | licence the case-by-case ruling ({CC}, "(other than X)" is one of the six questions decided site by site) and PLAN.md section 4.3 (sfad does not encode a rule about section 257)

§ `s 277(1AB) to (1AD): the Authority's declaration for a subsidiary of a listed entity`

-- src:44686 | (1AB) In relation to an offer of securities —
-- src:44688 | (a) where the securities are issued, whether by means of a
-- src:44689 | rights issue or otherwise, by a subsidiary (called in this
-- src:44690 | section the subsidiary) of an entity whose shares are listed
-- src:44691 | for quotation on an approved exchange (called in this
-- src:44692 | section the listed entity); and
-- src:44694 | (b) where the listed entity has guaranteed, or has agreed to
-- src:44695 | guarantee, unconditionally and irrevocably, all payment
-- src:44696 | obligations (whether in cash, in kind or otherwise) of the
-- src:44697 | subsidiary arising from the securities,
-- src:44699 | the Authority may, on the application of the subsidiary or the listed
-- src:44700 | entity, declare by written notice to the applicant that the provision of
-- src:44701 | an offer information statement in lieu of a prospectus relating to an
-- src:44702 | offer of securities would not be prejudicial to investors of such
-- src:44703 | securities.
@ref s 277(1AB) (src:44686-44703)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of securities?
    `the securities are issued, whether by means of a rights issue or otherwise, by a subsidiary of an entity whose shares are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities issued, whether by means of a rights issue or otherwise, by a subsidiary of an entity whose shares are listed for quotation on an approved exchange (the "listed entity")?
    `the listed entity has guaranteed, or has agreed to guarantee, unconditionally and irrevocably, all payment obligations of the subsidiary arising from the securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the listed entity guaranteed, or agreed to guarantee, unconditionally and irrevocably, all payment obligations (whether in cash, in kind or otherwise) of the subsidiary arising from the securities?
    `the subsidiary or the listed entity has applied to the Authority for the declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the subsidiary or the listed entity applied to the Authority for a declaration that the provision of an offer information statement in lieu of a prospectus would not be prejudicial to investors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1AB) the Authority may declare that the provision of an offer information statement in lieu of a prospectus would not be prejudicial to investors` MEANS
    IF `the offer is an offer of securities` AND `the securities are issued, whether by means of a rights issue or otherwise, by a subsidiary of an entity whose shares are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` AND `the listed entity has guaranteed, or has agreed to guarantee, unconditionally and irrevocably, all payment obligations of the subsidiary arising from the securities` AND `the subsidiary or the listed entity has applied to the Authority for the declaration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) where the securities are issued, whether by means of a rights issue or otherwise, by a subsidiary"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
    -- FORK s277-1AB | s 277(1AB) | `s 277(1AB) the Authority may declare that the provision of an offer information statement in lieu of a prospectus would not be prejudicial to investors` | took JUST FALSE where the subsidiary condition, the guarantee or the application is missing: the text opens "In relation to an offer of securities — (a) where ...; and (b) where ..." and then "on the application of the subsidiary or the listed entity", gates of the "where" and "on" kind, which the delegated-definitions ruling's item (c) counts as "where" and the periods ruling's item (b) answers JUST FALSE | other reading NOTHING (a function named for a power whose gate failed, limit 1 of the grant ruling) | licence {DEF-c} and {P-b}; {G3} says to list a "may" function with such a gate and not to change it: this is a split site (ii) of the brief. "On the application" is not named by the Guide itself: read by analogy with "upon" and listed under the marginal readings.

-- src:44713 | (a) the offer information statement relating to the offer of
-- src:44714 | securities —
-- src:44716 | (i) complies with such requirements as to form and
-- src:44717 | content as may be prescribed by regulations made
-- src:44718 | under section 341;
-- src:44723 | (ii) is signed by every director, or equivalent person, of
-- src:44724 | the subsidiary and the listed entity; and
-- src:44726 | (iii) is lodged by the subsidiary or the listed entity, with
-- src:44727 | the Authority;
@ref s 277(1AC)(a) (src:44713-44727)
GIVEN
    `the offer information statement complies with such requirements as to form and content as the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offer information statement relating to the offer of securities comply with the requirements as to form and content that the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
    `the offer information statement is signed by every director, or equivalent person, of the subsidiary and the listed entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer information statement signed by every director, or equivalent person, of the subsidiary and of the listed entity?
    `the offer information statement is lodged by the subsidiary or the listed entity with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer information statement lodged with the Authority by the subsidiary or the listed entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1AC)(a) the offer information statement meets the three requirements of paragraph (a)` MEANS
    IF `the offer information statement complies with such requirements as to form and content as the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341` AND `the offer information statement is signed by every director, or equivalent person, of the subsidiary and the listed entity` AND `the offer information statement is lodged by the subsidiary or the listed entity with the Authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if all of the following conditions are satisfied"

-- src:44729 | (b) either —
-- src:44731 | (i) the offer of securities is made in, or accompanied by,
-- src:44732 | the offer information statement mentioned in
-- src:44733 | paragraph (a); or
-- src:44735 | (ii) all the conditions in subsection (1B) are satisfied.
@ref s 277(1AC)(b) (src:44729-44735)
GIVEN
    `the offer of securities is made in, or accompanied by, the offer information statement mentioned in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer of securities made in, or accompanied by, the offer information statement mentioned in section 277(1AC)(a)?
    `the answer of subsection (1B)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 277(1B) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1AC)(b) the offer is made in or accompanied by the statement, or all the conditions in subsection (1B) are satisfied` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the offer of securities is made in, or accompanied by, the offer information statement mentioned in paragraph (a)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the answer of subsection (1B)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the answer of subsection (1B)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the conditions of subsection (1B) are satisfied is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "either — (i) the offer of securities is made in, or accompanied by, the offer information statement"

-- src:44707 | (1AC) Where the Authority makes a declaration mentioned in
-- src:44708 | subsection (1AB) in relation to an offer of securities, Subdivisions (2)
-- src:44709 | and (3) of this Division (other than section 257) do not apply to the
-- src:44710 | offer of securities for a period of 6 months starting on the date of the
-- src:44711 | declaration if all of the following conditions are satisfied:
@ref s 277(1AC) (src:44707-44711)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has made a declaration mentioned in subsection (1AB) in relation to the offer of securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority made a declaration under section 277(1AB) in relation to the offer of securities?
    `the day of the declaration` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Authority make the declaration?
    `the day the offer is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the offer of securities made?
    `the answer of paragraph (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 277(1AC)(a) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the answer of paragraph (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 277(1AC)(b) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1AC) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257) for 6 months from the declaration` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Authority has made a declaration mentioned in subsection (1AB) in relation to the offer of securities`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the Authority makes a declaration mentioned in subsection (1AB) in relation to an offer of securities"
        IF (`the day the offer is made` LESS THAN `the day of the declaration`) OR (`the day the offer is made` GREATER THAN (`period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the day of the declaration` 6 Months))
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply to the offer of securities for a period of 6 months starting on the date of the declaration"
        IF (`the answer of paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the answer of paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if all of the following conditions are satisfied"
        IF (`the answer of paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a condition is not answered
    -- FORK s277-1AC | s 277(1AC) | `s 277(1AC) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257) for 6 months from the declaration` | took the 6 months as beginning with the day of the declaration ("starting on the date of the declaration": keel P10), JUST FALSE outside the period (a period the text fixes in its own words) and where a condition fails ("if all of the following conditions are satisfied"), and NOTHING where no declaration has been made (the subsection speaks only of the case where the Authority makes one) | other reading JUST FALSE where no declaration has been made (a "where" condition, the periods ruling's item (b)) | licence {P-a}, {IN-SHORT} for the conditions, and {P-c} for the missing declaration. The "(other than section 257)" is left to the caller as at s 277(1) (fork s277-1-257).

-- src:44739 | (1AD) The Authority may, on making a declaration under
-- src:44740 | subsection (1AB), provide that the offer of securities may only be
-- src:44741 | made subject to such conditions or restrictions as the Authority may
-- src:44742 | impose.
@ref s 277(1AD) (src:44739-44742)
GIVEN
    `the Authority is making a declaration under subsection (1AB)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority making a declaration under section 277(1AB) about the offer of securities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(1AD) the Authority may provide that the offer may only be made subject to conditions or restrictions` MEANS
    IF `the Authority is making a declaration under subsection (1AB)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Authority may, on making a declaration under subsection (1AB), provide that the offer of securities may only be made subject to such conditions or restrictions as the Authority may impose"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
    -- FORK s277-1AD | s 277(1AD) | `s 277(1AD) the Authority may provide that the offer may only be made subject to conditions or restrictions` | took JUST FALSE where the Authority is not making a declaration: "on making" is a gate of the "where", "when", "upon" kind, which the delegated-definitions ruling's item (c) counts as "where", and the periods ruling's item (b) answers JUST FALSE for a failed "where" (the same words and the same answer as section 273(6)) | other reading NOTHING (a function named for a power whose gate failed, limit 1 of the grant ruling) | licence {DEF-c} and {P-b}; {G3} says to list a "may" function with such a gate and not to change it: this is a split site (ii) of the brief

§ `s 277(2) to (4): modification of the form and content, and the provisions applied to the statement`

-- src:44776 | (2) The Authority may, on the application of any person interested,
-- src:44777 | modify the prescribed form and content of the offer information
-- src:44778 | statement in such manner as is appropriate, subject to such conditions
-- src:44779 | or restrictions as the Authority may determine.
@ref s 277(2) (src:44776-44779)
GIVEN
    `a person interested has applied to the Authority to modify the prescribed form and content of the offer information statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person interested applied to the Authority to modify the form and content of the offer information statement that the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(2) the Authority may modify the prescribed form and content of the offer information statement` MEANS
    IF `a person interested has applied to the Authority to modify the prescribed form and content of the offer information statement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Authority may, on the application of any person interested, modify the prescribed form and content of the offer information statement"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
    -- FORK s277-2 | s 277(2) | `s 277(2) the Authority may modify the prescribed form and content of the offer information statement` | took JUST FALSE where no person interested has applied: "on the application of any person interested" is a gate of the "upon" kind (the delegated-definitions ruling's item (c) counts "upon" as "where") | other reading NOTHING (a function named for a power whose gate failed, limit 1 of the grant ruling) | licence {DEF-c} and {P-b}; {G3} says to list such a "may" function and not to change it: this is a split site (ii) of the brief. "On the application" is not named by the Guide itself: read by analogy with "upon" and listed under the marginal readings. The conditions or restrictions "as the Authority may determine" are the Authority's, outside the text.

-- src:44781 | (3) Sections 249, 249A, 253, 254 and 255 apply in relation to an
-- src:44782 | offer information statement referred to in subsection (1) or (1AC) as
-- src:44783 | they apply in relation to a prospectus.
@ref s 277(3) (src:44781-44783)
GIVEN
    `the document is an offer information statement referred to in subsection (1) or (1AC)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document an offer information statement referred to in section 277(1) or (1AC)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(3) sections 249, 249A, 253, 254 and 255 apply to the offer information statement as they apply to a prospectus` MEANS
    IF `the document is an offer information statement referred to in subsection (1) or (1AC)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to an offer information statement referred to in subsection (1) or (1AC)"

-- src:44787 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3) —
-- src:44789 | (a) a reference in section 249 or 249A to the registration of the
-- src:44790 | prospectus is to be read as a reference to the lodgment of
-- src:44791 | the offer information statement;
@ref s 277(4)(a) (src:44787-44791)
GIVEN
    `the provision is applied to an offer information statement under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision being applied to an offer information statement under section 277(3)?
    `the reference is a reference in section 249 or 249A to the registration of the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reference a reference in section 249 or 249A to the registration of the prospectus?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(4)(a) the reference to the registration of the prospectus is to be read as a reference to the lodgment of the offer information statement` MEANS
    IF `the provision is applied to an offer information statement under subsection (3)` AND `the reference is a reference in section 249 or 249A to the registration of the prospectus`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of subsection (3)"

-- src:44793 | (b) a reference in section 253 or 254 to any information or new
-- src:44794 | circumstance required to be included in a prospectus under
-- src:44795 | section 243 is to be read as a reference to any information
-- src:44796 | prescribed under subsection (1)(b); and
@ref s 277(4)(b) (src:44793-44796)
GIVEN
    `the provision is applied to an offer information statement under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision being applied to an offer information statement under section 277(3)?
    `the reference is a reference in section 253 or 254 to any information or new circumstance required to be included in a prospectus under section 243` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reference a reference in section 253 or 254 to any information or new circumstance required to be included in a prospectus under section 243?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(4)(b) the reference to information required in a prospectus is to be read as a reference to the information prescribed under subsection (1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the provision is applied to an offer information statement under subsection (3)` AND `the reference is a reference in section 253 or 254 to any information or new circumstance required to be included in a prospectus under section 243`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of subsection (3)"

-- src:44798 | (c) in relation to an offer information statement mentioned in
-- src:44799 | subsection (1AC), a reference in section 253(4)(a), (b) or
-- src:44800 | (c) or 254(3)(a), (b) or (c) to the person making the offer is
-- src:44801 | to be read as a reference to the subsidiary and the listed
-- src:44802 | entity.
@ref s 277(4)(c) (src:44798-44802)
GIVEN
    `the provision is applied to an offer information statement under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision being applied to an offer information statement under section 277(3)?
    `the statement is an offer information statement mentioned in subsection (1AC)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement an offer information statement mentioned in section 277(1AC)?
    `the reference is a reference in section 253(4)(a), (b) or (c) or 254(3)(a), (b) or (c) to the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reference a reference in section 253(4)(a), (b) or (c) or 254(3)(a), (b) or (c) to the person making the offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(4)(c) the reference to the person making the offer is to be read as a reference to the subsidiary and the listed entity` MEANS
    IF `the provision is applied to an offer information statement under subsection (3)` AND `the statement is an offer information statement mentioned in subsection (1AC)` AND `the reference is a reference in section 253(4)(a), (b) or (c) or 254(3)(a), (b) or (c) to the person making the offer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to an offer information statement mentioned in subsection (1AC)"

§ `s 277(5) and (6): the written consents lodged with the statement`


-- src:44806 | (5) Where the written consent of an expert is required to be given
-- src:44807 | under section 249 (as applied in relation to an offer information
-- src:44808 | statement under subsection (3)), that written consent must be lodged
-- src:44809 | with the Authority at the same time as the lodgment of the statement.
@ref s 277(5) (src:44806-44809)
GIVEN
    `the written consent of an expert is required to be given under section 249, as applied in relation to an offer information statement under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the written consent of an expert required to be given under section 249, as applied in relation to an offer information statement under section 277(3)?
    `the day the written consent of the expert is lodged with the Authority` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the expert's written consent lodged with the Authority?
    `the day the offer information statement is lodged` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the offer information statement lodged with the Authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(5) the written consent of the expert is lodged with the Authority at the same time as the lodgment of the statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the written consent of an expert is required to be given under section 249, as applied in relation to an offer information statement under subsection (3)`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the written consent of an expert is required to be given under section 249"
        IF `the day the written consent of the expert is lodged with the Authority` EQUALS `the day the offer information statement is lodged`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that written consent must be lodged with the Authority at the same time as the lodgment of the statement"
    -- FORK s277-5 | s 277(5) | `s 277(5) the written consent of the expert is lodged with the Authority at the same time as the lodgment of the statement` | took "at the same time" as the same day (the text counts no unit finer than a day and this encoding takes dates) and NOTHING where no consent is required (the question is whether the duty was met; the "Where" gate, if unmet, leaves no duty to meet) | other reading JUST FALSE where no consent is required, or the same instant rather than the same day | licence {CC} (a duty whose "where" is unmet, decided site by site) and the text's own words. No party is named (the text says only that the consent "must be lodged"), so there is no regulative rule here: the duty is listed under "Rules with no breach path".

-- src:44811 | (6) Where the written consent of an issue manager or underwriter is
-- src:44812 | required to be given under section 249A (as applied in relation to an
-- src:44813 | offer information statement under subsection (3)), that written
-- src:44814 | consent must be lodged with the Authority at the same time as the
-- src:44815 | lodgment of the statement.
@ref s 277(6) (src:44811-44815)
GIVEN
    `the written consent of an issue manager or underwriter is required to be given under section 249A, as applied in relation to an offer information statement under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the written consent of an issue manager or underwriter required to be given under section 249A, as applied in relation to an offer information statement under section 277(3)?
    `the day the written consent of the issue manager or underwriter is lodged with the Authority` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the issue manager's or underwriter's written consent lodged with the Authority?
    `the day the offer information statement is lodged` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the offer information statement lodged with the Authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(6) the written consent of the issue manager or underwriter is lodged with the Authority at the same time as the lodgment of the statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the written consent of an issue manager or underwriter is required to be given under section 249A, as applied in relation to an offer information statement under subsection (3)`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the written consent of an issue manager or underwriter is required to be given under section 249A"
        IF `the day the written consent of the issue manager or underwriter is lodged with the Authority` EQUALS `the day the offer information statement is lodged`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that written consent must be lodged with the Authority at the same time as the lodgment of the statement"
    -- FORK s277-6 | s 277(6) | `s 277(6) the written consent of the issue manager or underwriter is lodged with the Authority at the same time as the lodgment of the statement` | took the same readings as section 277(5): the same day, and NOTHING where no consent is required | other reading JUST FALSE where no consent is required, or the same instant rather than the same day | licence {CC} (a duty whose "where" is unmet, decided site by site) and the text's own words. No party is named, so there is no regulative rule here: the duty is listed under "Rules with no breach path".

§ `s 277(7) and (8): the bar on advertising or publishing, and the offence`


-- src:44817 | (7) A person must not advertise an offer or intended offer of any
-- src:44818 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts referred to in
-- src:44819 | subsection (1) or (1AC), or publish a statement that directly or
-- src:44820 | indirectly refers to the offer or intended offer, or that is reasonably
-- src:44825 | likely to induce persons to subscribe for or purchase the securities or
-- src:44826 | securities‑based derivatives contracts, unless the advertisement or
-- src:44827 | publication complies with such requirements as the Authority may
-- src:44828 | prescribe by regulations made under section 341.
@ref s 277(7) (src:44817-44828)
GIVEN
    `the person advertises an offer or intended offer of securities or contracts referred to in subsection (1) or (1AC)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person advertise an offer or intended offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts referred to in section 277(1) or (1AC)?
    `the person publishes a statement that directly or indirectly refers to the offer or intended offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person publish a statement that, directly or indirectly, refers to the offer or intended offer?
    `the person publishes a statement that is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe for or purchase the securities or contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person publish a statement that is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe for or purchase the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the advertisement or publication complies with the requirements prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertisement or publication comply with the requirements the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(7) the person must not advertise or publish what the subsection bars` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person advertises an offer or intended offer of securities or contracts referred to in subsection (1) or (1AC)` OR `the person publishes a statement that directly or indirectly refers to the offer or intended offer` OR `the person publishes a statement that is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe for or purchase the securities or contracts`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of an advertisement or a statement of the kinds it names
        IF `the advertisement or publication complies with the requirements prescribed by regulations made under section 341`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the advertisement or publication complies with such requirements as the Authority may prescribe by regulations made under section 341"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:44834 | (8) Any person who contravenes subsection (7), or who knowingly
-- src:44835 | authorises or permits the publication or dissemination of any
-- src:44836 | advertisement or statement referred to in that subsection, shall be
-- src:44837 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:44838 | exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:44839 | 12 months or to both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- src:44840 | further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:44841 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 277(8) (src:44834-44841)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene section 277(7)?
    `the person knowingly authorises or permits the publication or dissemination of an advertisement or statement referred to in subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person knowingly authorise or permit the publication or dissemination of an advertisement or statement referred to in section 277(7)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 277(8) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes subsection (7)` OR `the person knowingly authorises or permits the publication or dissemination of an advertisement or statement referred to in subsection (7)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any person who contravenes subsection (7), or who knowingly authorises or permits the publication or dissemination of any advertisement or statement referred to in that subsection, shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
    -- FORK s277-8 | s 277(8) | `s 277(8) the person is guilty of an offence` | took JUST FALSE where neither element is shown (this provision's own question) | other reading NOTHING | licence {G2} and the brief's split site (i)

@ref s 277(8) (src:44834-44841)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 277(8) the penalty for the offence` MEANS Penalty OF 50000, 12, TRUE, 5000

§ `s 277: the bar of subsection (7) as a regulative rule`

DECLARE `s 277 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 277 a person`

DECLARE `s 277 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 277(7) advertise or publish what the subsection bars`

-- src:44817 | (7) A person must not advertise an offer or intended offer of any
-- src:44818 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts referred to in
-- src:44819 | subsection (1) or (1AC), or publish a statement that directly or
@ref s 277(7) (src:44817-44819)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 277 party` `s 277 act`
`s 277(7) the bar on advertising or publishing` MEANS
    PARTY `s 277 a person`
    SHANT `s 277(7) advertise or publish what the subsection bars`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 277 a person` BECAUSE "the person advertised or published what section 277(7) bars, without complying with the requirements prescribed under section 341"

§ `s 278: offer in respect of international debentures`

-- src:44852 | (a) is made by the holder of a capital markets services licence
-- src:44853 | to deal in capital markets products that are securities or
-- src:44854 | securities‑based derivatives contracts or an exempt person
-- src:44855 | under section 99(1)(a) or (b), to such institutional,
-- src:44856 | professional or business investors as the Authority may,
-- src:44857 | by order in the Gazette, specify, being persons or bodies
-- src:44858 | that appear to the Authority to have sufficient expertise to
-- src:44859 | understand any risk involved in buying or selling those
-- src:44860 | debentures, or units of debentures (whether as principal or
-- src:44861 | agent); and
@ref s 278(1)(a) (src:44852-44861)
GIVEN
    `the offer is made by the holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made by the holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the offer is made by an exempt person under section 99(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made by an exempt person under section 99(1)(a) or (b)?
    `the offer is made to investors of a kind that the Authority has specified by order in the Gazette as institutional, professional or business investors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made to such institutional, professional or business investors as the Authority has specified by order in the Gazette?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278(1)(a) the offer is made by a licensee or an exempt person to the investors the Authority has specified` MEANS
    IF (`the offer is made by the holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` OR `the offer is made by an exempt person under section 99(1)(a) or (b)`) AND `the offer is made to investors of a kind that the Authority has specified by order in the Gazette as institutional, professional or business investors`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the offer — (a) is made by the holder of a capital markets services licence"
    -- FORK s278-1a | s 278(1)(a) | `s 278(1)(a) the offer is made by a licensee or an exempt person to the investors the Authority has specified` | took "being persons or bodies that appear to the Authority to have sufficient expertise to understand any risk involved" as the Authority's reason for specifying the investors, not a second condition the caller must show (the specification by order in the Gazette is the fact asked) | other reading a separate condition that the investors appear to the Authority to have sufficient expertise | licence the text's own words: "such institutional, professional or business investors as the Authority may, by order in the Gazette, specify, being persons or bodies that appear to the Authority"

-- src:44867 | (2) The conditions referred to in subsection (1)(b) are that —
-- src:44869 | (a) the debentures, or units of debentures, are denominated in a
-- src:44870 | currency, other than the Singapore dollar, and each
-- src:44875 | debenture, or each unit of debenture, has a face value of at
-- src:44876 | least US$5,000 or its equivalent in another currency; and
@ref s 278(2)(a) (src:44867-44876)
GIVEN
    `the debentures, or units of debentures, are denominated in a currency other than the Singapore dollar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the debentures, or units of debentures, denominated in a currency other than the Singapore dollar?
    `the lowest face value of any debenture, or unit of debenture, in the offer, in United States dollars or the equivalent in another currency` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lowest face value of any debenture, or unit of debenture, in the offer, in United States dollars (or its equivalent in another currency)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278(2)(a) the debentures are denominated in a foreign currency and each has a face value of at least US$5,000` MEANS
    IF `the debentures, or units of debentures, are denominated in a currency other than the Singapore dollar` AND (`the lowest face value of any debenture, or unit of debenture, in the offer, in United States dollars or the equivalent in another currency` AT LEAST 5000)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions referred to in subsection (1)(b) are that"
    -- FORK s278-2a | s 278(2)(a) | `s 278(2)(a) the debentures are denominated in a foreign currency and each has a face value of at least US$5,000` | took "each debenture, or each unit of debenture, has a face value of at least US$5,000 or its equivalent" as a test on the lowest face value in the offer, in United States dollars or the equivalent (the conversion is the caller's) | other reading a test on the face value of each debenture one by one, which gives the same answer | licence the text's own words. The figure US$5,000 is the text's own; the Authority may vary it by order under section 278(3), which is outside the text (a caller who knows of a varied figure applies it themselves).

-- src:44878 | (b) the shares of the issuing corporation are listed on a
-- src:44879 | recognised securities exchange or the offer is guaranteed
-- src:44880 | by a corporation whose shares are listed on a recognised
-- src:44881 | securities exchange.
@ref s 278(2)(b) (src:44878-44881)
GIVEN
    `the shares of the issuing corporation are listed on a recognised securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares of the issuing corporation listed on a recognised securities exchange?
    `the offer is guaranteed by a corporation whose shares are listed on a recognised securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer guaranteed by a corporation whose shares are listed on a recognised securities exchange?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278(2)(b) the shares of the issuing corporation, or of a guarantor, are listed on a recognised securities exchange` MEANS
    IF `the shares of the issuing corporation are listed on a recognised securities exchange` OR `the offer is guaranteed by a corporation whose shares are listed on a recognised securities exchange`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions referred to in subsection (1)(b) are that"

-- src:44867 | (2) The conditions referred to in subsection (1)(b) are that —
@ref s 278(2) (src:44867-44867)
GIVEN
    `the answer of paragraph (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 278(2)(a) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the answer of paragraph (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 278(2)(b) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278(2) the offer complies with the conditions specified in this subsection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the answer of paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the answer of paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the answer of paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions referred to in subsection (1)(b) are that"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a condition is not answered

-- src:44863 | (b) complies with the conditions specified in subsection (2).
@ref s 278(1)(b) (src:44863-44863)
GIVEN
    `the answer of subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 278(2) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278(1)(b) the offer complies with the conditions specified in subsection (2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of subsection (2)`
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the offer complies with the conditions of subsection (2) is not known

-- src:44847 | 278.—(1) Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division (other than
-- src:44848 | section 257) do not apply to an offer of debentures, or units of
-- src:44849 | debentures, by a body incorporated in a country outside Singapore
-- src:44850 | where the offer —
@ref s 278(1) (src:44847-44850)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of debentures, or units of debentures, by a body incorporated in a country outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of debentures, or units of debentures, by a body incorporated in a country outside Singapore?
    `the answer of paragraph (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 278(1)(a) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the answer of paragraph (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 278(1)(b) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278(1) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offer is an offer of debentures, or units of debentures, by a body incorporated in a country outside Singapore`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offer of debentures, or units of debentures, by a body incorporated in a country outside Singapore"
        IF (`the answer of paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the answer of paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the offer —"
        IF (`the answer of paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a paragraph is not answered
    -- FORK s278-1 | s 278(1) | `s 278(1) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` | took NOTHING where the offer is not by a body incorporated outside Singapore or is not of debentures (a scope limit with no "only") and JUST FALSE where paragraph (a) or (b) fails (a "where" condition on the exemption, which is not a "may") | other reading JUST FALSE for the scope too | licence {P-c} for the scope, {P-b} for the "where" paragraphs. "(other than section 257)" is left to the caller as at section 277(1) (fork s277-1-257).

-- src:44883 | (3) The Authority may by order in the Gazette add to, vary or
-- src:44884 | amend the conditions specified in subsection (2).
@ref s 278(3) (src:44883-44884)
GIVEN
    `the Authority acts by order in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Authority act by order in the Gazette?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278(3) the Authority may add to, vary or amend the conditions specified in subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the Authority acts by order in the Gazette`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Authority may by order in the Gazette add to, vary or amend the conditions specified in subsection (2)"
    -- FORK s278-3 | s 278(3) | `s 278(3) the Authority may add to, vary or amend the conditions specified in subsection (2)` | took NOTHING where the Authority does not act by order in the Gazette (the text limits the power to that manner and does not say what the Authority may do otherwise) | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {G1}; "by order in the Gazette" is a manner, not a gate of the "where", "when" or "upon" kind, so this is not a split site

§ `s 279: offer of debentures made by the Government or an international financial institution`

-- src:44889 | 279. Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division do not apply to an
-- src:44890 | offer of debentures, or units of debentures, made by or guaranteed
-- src:44891 | by —
-- src:44893 | (a) the Government; or
-- src:44895 | (b) an international financial institution in which Singapore
-- src:44896 | holds membership of any class or description, whether or
-- src:44897 | not it holds any share in the share capital of that institution.
@ref s 279 (src:44889-44897)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of debentures, or units of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of debentures, or units of debentures?
    `the offer is made by or guaranteed by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made by or guaranteed by the Government?
    `the offer is made by or guaranteed by an international financial institution in which Singapore holds membership of any class or description` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made by or guaranteed by an international financial institution in which Singapore holds membership of any class or description, whether or not it holds any share in the share capital of that institution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279 the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division` MEANS
    IF `the offer is an offer of debentures, or units of debentures` AND (`the offer is made by or guaranteed by the Government` OR `the offer is made by or guaranteed by an international financial institution in which Singapore holds membership of any class or description`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "do not apply to an offer of debentures, or units of debentures, made by or guaranteed by"
    -- FORK s279 | s 279 | `s 279 the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division` | took NOTHING where the offer is not made or guaranteed by the Government or such an institution (a scope limit with no "only", and the list of persons is not closed with "only") | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {P-c}. Unlike sections 277 and 278 this section does not say "(other than section 257)": it names Subdivisions (2) and (3) only, and the function says so.

§ `s 280: offer made using an automated teller machine or other electronic means`

-- src:44902 | 280.—(1) Subject to subsection (3) and such requirements as the
-- src:44903 | Authority may prescribe, a person making an offer of securities or
-- src:44904 | securities‑based derivatives contracts using —
-- src:44906 | (a) any automated teller machine; or
-- src:44908 | (b) such other electronic means as the Authority may
-- src:44909 | prescribe,
-- src:44911 | is exempted from the requirement under section 240(1)(a) that the
-- src:44912 | offer be made in or accompanied by a prospectus in respect of the
-- src:44913 | offer or, where applicable, the requirement under section 240(4) that
-- src:44914 | the offer be made in or accompanied by a profile statement in respect
-- src:44915 | of the offer.
@ref s 280(1) (src:44902-44915)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the offer is made using an automated teller machine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made using an automated teller machine?
    `the offer is made using other electronic means that the Authority has prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made using electronic means, other than an automated teller machine, that the Authority has prescribed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 280(1) the offer is an offer referred to in section 280` MEANS
    `the offer is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` AND (`the offer is made using an automated teller machine` OR `the offer is made using other electronic means that the Authority has prescribed`)

@ref s 280(1) (src:44902-44915)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer one made using an automated teller machine, or other electronic means the Authority has prescribed? (This is what the function for section 280(1) "the offer is an offer referred to in section 280" answers.)
    `the person making the offer complies with the requirements the Authority has prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person making the offer comply with such requirements as the Authority has prescribed?
    `the answer of subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 280(3) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 280(1) the person making the offer is exempted from the requirement of a prospectus or profile statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offer is an offer referred to in subsection (1)`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person making an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts using — (a) any automated teller machine; or (b) such other electronic means as the Authority may prescribe"
        IF `the answer of subsection (3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply unless"
        IF NOT `the person making the offer complies with the requirements the Authority has prescribed`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (3) and such requirements as the Authority may prescribe"
        IF `the answer of subsection (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether subsection (3) is met is not known
    -- FORK s280-1 | s 280(1) | `s 280(1) the person making the offer is exempted from the requirement of a prospectus or profile statement` | took JUST FALSE where the prescribed requirements are not complied with: "Subject to ... such requirements as the Authority may prescribe" is read as the text's own condition, a plain variant of "if" | other reading NOTHING ("subject to" is not one of the words the "In short" sentence lists, and the requirements are outside the text) | licence {IN-SHORT} ("plain variants" of "if"). The requirement exempted from, section 240(1)(a) and (4), is Subdivision (2)'s and another part's; the function does not call it (PLAN.md section 4.3).

-- src:44919 | (2) To avoid doubt, a prospectus which complies with all other
-- src:44920 | requirements of section 240(1)(a) or, where applicable, a profile
-- src:44925 | statement which complies with all other requirements of
-- src:44926 | section 240(4) must still be prepared and issued in respect of any
-- src:44927 | offer referred to in subsection (1).
@ref s 280(2) (src:44919-44927)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer one made using an automated teller machine, or other electronic means the Authority has prescribed? (This is what the function for section 280(1) "the offer is an offer referred to in section 280" answers.)
    `a prospectus complying with all other requirements of section 240(1)(a), or where applicable a profile statement complying with all other requirements of section 240(4), has been prepared and issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a prospectus complying with all other requirements of section 240(1)(a), or where applicable a profile statement complying with all other requirements of section 240(4), been prepared and issued for the offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 280(2) a prospectus or profile statement complying with the other requirements has been prepared and issued for the offer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offer is an offer referred to in subsection (1)`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of any offer referred to in subsection (1)"
        IF `a prospectus complying with all other requirements of section 240(1)(a), or where applicable a profile statement complying with all other requirements of section 240(4), has been prepared and issued`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must still be prepared and issued in respect of any offer referred to in subsection (1)"
    -- FORK s280-2 | s 280(2) | `s 280(2) a prospectus or profile statement complying with the other requirements has been prepared and issued for the offer` | took the function as the compliance question (JUST TRUE where it has been prepared and issued, JUST FALSE where it has not) and NOTHING for an offer that is not one referred to in subsection (1) | other reading the function answers "is a prospectus still required" (always JUST TRUE for such an offer) | licence the text's own words ("must still be prepared and issued") and {CC}. No party is named and no time is given, so there is no regulative rule here: the duty is listed under "Rules with no breach path".

-- src:44929 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply unless the automated teller
-- src:44930 | machine or prescribed electronic means indicates to a prospective
-- src:44931 | subscriber or buyer —
-- src:44933 | (a) how the prospective subscriber or buyer can obtain, or
-- src:44934 | arrange to receive, a copy of the prospectus or, where
-- src:44935 | applicable, profile statement in respect of the offer; and
-- src:44937 | (b) that the prospective subscriber or buyer should read the
-- src:44938 | prospectus or, where applicable, profile statement before
-- src:44939 | submitting an application,
-- src:44941 | before enabling the prospective subscriber or buyer to submit any
-- src:44942 | application to subscribe for or purchase securities or securities‑based
-- src:44943 | derivatives contracts.
@ref s 280(3) (src:44929-44943)
GIVEN
    `the machine or the prescribed electronic means indicates to a prospective subscriber or buyer how to obtain, or arrange to receive, a copy of the prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the automated teller machine or the prescribed electronic means indicate to a prospective subscriber or buyer how they can obtain, or arrange to receive, a copy of the prospectus or, where applicable, profile statement in respect of the offer?
    `the machine or the prescribed electronic means indicates to a prospective subscriber or buyer that they should read the prospectus or profile statement before submitting an application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the automated teller machine or the prescribed electronic means indicate to a prospective subscriber or buyer that they should read the prospectus or, where applicable, profile statement before submitting an application?
    `the indications are given before enabling the prospective subscriber or buyer to submit any application to subscribe for or purchase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those indications given before the prospective subscriber or buyer is enabled to submit any application to subscribe for or purchase securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 280(3) the machine or the electronic means gives the indications that subsection (1) needs` MEANS
    IF `the machine or the prescribed electronic means indicates to a prospective subscriber or buyer how to obtain, or arrange to receive, a copy of the prospectus or profile statement` AND `the machine or the prescribed electronic means indicates to a prospective subscriber or buyer that they should read the prospectus or profile statement before submitting an application` AND `the indications are given before enabling the prospective subscriber or buyer to submit any application to subscribe for or purchase`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply unless"

§ `s 280A: information relating to certain offers`

-- src:44949 | 280A. The Authority may, by regulations made under section 341,
-- src:44950 | require any person or class of persons to provide the Authority with
-- src:44951 | such information relating to an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:44952 | derivatives contracts made or proposed to be made in reliance on an
-- src:44953 | exemption under any provision of this Subdivision.
@ref s 280A (src:44949-44953)
GIVEN
    `the information relates to an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts made or proposed to be made in reliance on an exemption under a provision of this Subdivision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information relate to an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts made, or proposed to be made, in reliance on an exemption under a provision of Subdivision (4) of Division 1 of Part 13?
    `the Authority acts by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Authority act by regulations made under section 341?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 280A the Authority may require a person or class of persons to provide information about an offer made in reliance on an exemption` MEANS
    IF `the information relates to an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts made or proposed to be made in reliance on an exemption under a provision of this Subdivision` AND `the Authority acts by regulations made under section 341`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, by regulations made under section 341, require any person or class of persons to provide the Authority with such information"
    -- FORK s280A | s 280A | `s 280A the Authority may require a person or class of persons to provide information about an offer made in reliance on an exemption` | took NOTHING where the information is about another kind of offer or the Authority does not act by regulations (the text limits the power to that subject and that manner) | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {G1}; neither limit is a gate of the "where", "when" or "upon" kind, so this is not a split site. Which persons and what information the regulations name is outside the text.

§ `s 281: revocation of exemption`

-- src:44959 | 281.—(1) Where the Authority considers that a person is
-- src:44960 | contravening, or is likely to contravene, or has contravened any
-- src:44961 | condition or restriction imposed under section 273(6), or that it is
-- src:44962 | necessary in the public interest or for the protection of investors, it
-- src:44963 | may revoke any exemption under this Subdivision, subject to such
-- src:44964 | conditions as it thinks fit.
@ref s 281(1) (src:44959-44964)
GIVEN
    `the Authority considers that a person is contravening, or is likely to contravene, or has contravened a condition or restriction imposed under section 273(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Authority consider that a person is contravening, or is likely to contravene, or has contravened any condition or restriction imposed under section 273(6)?
    `the Authority considers that it is necessary in the public interest or for the protection of investors to revoke the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Authority consider that it is necessary in the public interest or for the protection of investors to revoke the exemption?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 281(1) the Authority may revoke an exemption under this Subdivision` MEANS
    IF `the Authority considers that a person is contravening, or is likely to contravene, or has contravened a condition or restriction imposed under section 273(6)` OR `the Authority considers that it is necessary in the public interest or for the protection of investors to revoke the exemption`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the Authority considers that a person is contravening, or is likely to contravene, or has contravened any condition or restriction imposed under section 273(6)"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
    -- FORK s281-1 | s 281(1) | `s 281(1) the Authority may revoke an exemption under this Subdivision` | took NOTHING where the Authority has formed neither view: the gate "Where the Authority considers ..." is the Authority's own opinion, a standard for exercising its power, not a fact the caller can show to be absent, and the text does not say what the Authority may do when it holds neither view | other reading JUST FALSE (the text says "Where", and the periods ruling's item (b) says a failed "where" condition answers JUST FALSE) | licence the grant ruling's limit 1 ({G1}: NOTHING for a power whose gate failed; the "In short" sentence: "limits a grant or prohibition in its own wording and the case falls outside the limit"); {G3} says to list a "may" function whose gate is "where" and not to change it: this is a split site (ii) of the brief, answered differently from sections 277(1AB), (1AD) and (2) because those gates are an application or a declaration the caller can show absent, and this one is the Authority's own state of mind. Listed under the marginal readings.

-- src:44966 | (2) The Authority may revoke an exemption under subsection (1)
-- src:44967 | without giving the person affected by the revocation an opportunity to
-- src:44968 | be heard, but the person may, within 14 days of the revocation, apply
@ref s 281(2) (src:44966-44968)
GIVEN
    `the Authority revokes an exemption under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Authority revoke an exemption under section 281(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 281(2) the Authority may revoke the exemption without giving the person affected an opportunity to be heard` MEANS
    IF `the Authority revokes an exemption under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Authority may revoke an exemption under subsection (1) without giving the person affected by the revocation an opportunity to be heard"

-- src:44966 | (2) The Authority may revoke an exemption under subsection (1)
-- src:44967 | without giving the person affected by the revocation an opportunity to
-- src:44968 | be heard, but the person may, within 14 days of the revocation, apply
-- src:44969 | to the Authority for the revocation to be reviewed by the Authority,
@ref s 281(2) (src:44966-44969)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has revoked an exemption under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority revoked an exemption under section 281(1)?
    `the day of the revocation` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the exemption revoked?
    `the day the person applies for the revocation to be reviewed` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the person affected apply to the Authority for the revocation to be reviewed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 281(2) the person may apply to the Authority for the revocation to be reviewed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Authority has revoked an exemption under subsection (1)`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person may, within 14 days of the revocation, apply to the Authority for the revocation to be reviewed"
        IF (`the day the person applies for the revocation to be reviewed` AT LEAST `the day of the revocation`) AND (`period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the revocation` `the day the person applies for the revocation to be reviewed` 14 Days)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days of the revocation, apply to the Authority for the revocation to be reviewed"
    -- FORK s281-2 | s 281(2) | `s 281(2) the person may apply to the Authority for the revocation to be reviewed` | took the 14 days as running from the day of the revocation (keel P1: the day of the revocation is not counted as day 1, so the last day is the 14th day after it) with an application on the day of the revocation itself in time (the keel's "not later than the end of a period after", not its "within a period after" window, which opens the day after, P2: the text says "within 14 days of", and a person who applies on the day of the revocation is evidently within 14 days of it), and JUST FALSE outside it, because "within 14 days" is a period the text fixes in its own words; NOTHING where nothing has been revoked | other reading the keel's P2 window, which opens the day after the revocation, so that an application on the day of the revocation is out of time | licence {P-a} (a period the text fixes in its own words). "Within 14 days" is a period, not a gate of the "where", "when" or "upon" kind, so this is not a split site.

-- src:44974 | and the revocation remains in effect unless it is withdrawn by the
-- src:44975 | Authority.
@ref s 281(2) (src:44974-44975)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has revoked an exemption under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority revoked an exemption under section 281(1)?
    `the Authority has withdrawn the revocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority withdrawn the revocation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 281(2) the revocation remains in effect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Authority has revoked an exemption under subsection (1)`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and the revocation remains in effect unless it is withdrawn by the Authority"
        IF `the Authority has withdrawn the revocation`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the revocation remains in effect unless it is withdrawn by the Authority"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    -- FORK s281-2e | s 281(2) | `s 281(2) the revocation remains in effect` | took the revocation as remaining in effect whether or not the person has applied for a review (the text says it "remains in effect unless it is withdrawn by the Authority", and does not make the application a ground for it to lapse) | other reading an application for review suspends the revocation | licence the text's own words ("unless")

-- src:44977 | (3) A revocation made under this section is final and there is no
-- src:44978 | appeal from the revocation.
@ref s 281(3) (src:44977-44978)
GIVEN
    `the revocation is made under this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the revocation made under section 281?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 281(3) the revocation is final and no appeal lies from it` MEANS
    IF `the revocation is made under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A revocation made under this section is final and there is no appeal from the revocation"

§ `s 282: transactions under exempted offers remain subject to Division 2 of Part 12 of the Companies Act 1967 and Part 12 of this Act`

-- src:44983 | 282. To avoid doubt, it is declared that in relation to any transaction
-- src:44984 | carried out under an exempted offer under this Part, nothing in this
-- src:44985 | Part limits or diminishes any liability which any person may incur in
-- src:44986 | respect of any relevant offence under Division 2 of Part 12 of the
-- src:44987 | Companies Act 1967 or Part 12 of this Act or any penalty, award of
-- src:44988 | compensation or punishment in respect of any such offence.
@ref s 282 (src:44983-44988)
GIVEN
    `the transaction is carried out under an exempted offer under Part 13` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction one carried out under an exempted offer under Part 13 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001?
    `the liability, penalty, award of compensation or punishment is in respect of a relevant offence under Division 2 of Part 12 of the Companies Act 1967 or Part 12 of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability, or the penalty, award of compensation or punishment, in respect of a relevant offence under Division 2 of Part 12 of the Companies Act 1967 or Part 12 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 282 nothing in this Part limits or diminishes the liability` MEANS
    IF `the transaction is carried out under an exempted offer under Part 13` AND `the liability, penalty, award of compensation or punishment is in respect of a relevant offence under Division 2 of Part 12 of the Companies Act 1967 or Part 12 of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to any transaction carried out under an exempted offer under this Part, nothing in this Part limits or diminishes any liability"
    -- FORK s282 | s 282 | `s 282 nothing in this Part limits or diminishes the liability` | took the declaration as a rule that preserves a liability (JUST TRUE where both facts are shown) and NOTHING otherwise: it declares what this Part does not do and is silent on every other transaction | other reading an inert row (a declaration "to avoid doubt" that adds no rule) | licence {IN-SHORT} (silent). Whether an offence is a "relevant offence" is for Part 12 and the Companies Act 1967, outside this text.
